#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This dataset was made to show a fake vehicle making a sharp turn. With rear wheels that are not steered, the rear axle should follow the target path and should not move laterally at all relative to the path. (On the other hand, the front axle can move laterally due to presumed steering.)
#
#The X coordinates of the shape are offset by the X length (2.690 m). Instead of X=0 being at the front axle (for most shadows), it is at the rear axle.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

